ion: the whole point is that under ~10 parallel reviews 'the volume fills anyway' — fail-open on an unwritable store on the t4g.large restores that exposure precisely when the store cannot be written"],"finding":"The 'fail OPEN on every plumbing failure' choice silently disarms the concurrency cap when the slot store is unwritable, with no observability signal on that path — reintroducing the exact bug-3276 volume-fill under the fault the cap exists to prevent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f394b19bcaeaa69ad","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design → Counter ('Every plumbing failure (no `fcntl`, unwritable store) fails OPEN.')","norm_id":"ndfc4a709f71a0212","priority":0.875,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The snapshot locks/ directory or REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR volume becomes unwritable/full on the production box; the cap silently no-ops and admits all ~10 concurrent gates","An operator inspecting journald sees neither a congestion refusal nor any signal that the bound has stopped engaging"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a distinct best-effort stderr marker (e.g. GATE_ADMISSION_DISARMED {json} naming the reason) on the fail-open path, and add a sentence of positive rationale in the design comment for why admission fails open rather than refusing when its own store is unusable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion asserting admission fails OPEN (gate proceeds) when the slot store is unwritable or fcntl is unavailable, rather than crashing the gate.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b","E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a malformed or negative value falls back to the default rather than disarming the cap or crashing every gate'","'Every plumbing failure (no fcntl, unwritable store) fails OPEN.'","AC1–AC7 cover admission, refusal, config, docs, metric — none covers the no-fcntl / unwritable-store fail-open arm"],"finding":"The plan makes 'fail OPEN on plumbing failure (no fcntl, unwritable store)' a load-bearing safety behavior but no acceptance criterion exercises it; the admitted/refused paths are tested (AC1–AC7) while the degraded fail-open path — which decides whether a broken store crashes every gate or admits it — is unverified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6bdea29304d4d4b6","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design — Counter; Acceptance Criteria (no AC for fail-open)","norm_id":"n6fcd079c243054d3","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An unwritable REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR or missing fcntl at runtime: the intended fail-open is asserted in prose but a regression that turns it into a crash-closed (every gate fails) would ship undetected"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add AC8: simulate an unwritable locks/ dir (and/or absent fcntl) and assert the gate is